{"id":"heaven","name":"Heaven","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","torrey","easton"],"topics":["nave:heaven","torrey:heaven"],"groups":["The Future Dwelling Place Of The Righteous"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Heaven","text":"(1.) Definitions. The phrase “heaven and earth” is used to indicate the whole universe (Gen. 1:1; Jer. 23:24; Acts 17:24). According to the Jewish notion there were three heavens, (a) The firmament, as “fowls of the heaven” (Gen. 2:19; 7:3, 23; Ps. 8:8, etc.), “the eagles of heaven” (Lam. 4:19), etc. (b) The starry heavens (Deut. 17:3; Jer. 8:2; Matt. 24:29). (c) “The heaven of heavens,” or “the third heaven” (Deut. 10:14; 1 Kings 8:27; Ps. 115:16; 148:4; 2 Cor. 12:2). (2.) Meaning of words in the original, (a) The usual Hebrew word for “heavens” is shamayim, a plural form meaning “heights,” “elevations” (Gen. 1:1; 2:1). (b) The Hebrew word marom is also used (Ps. 68:18; 93:4; 102:19, etc.) as equivalent to shamayim, “high places,” “heights.” (c) Heb. galgal, literally a “wheel,” is rendered “heaven” in Ps. 77:18 (R.V., “whirlwind”). (d) Heb. shahak, rendered “sky” (Deut. 33:26; Job …"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H8064","lemma":"שָׁמַיִם","xlit":"shâmayim","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, astrologer, heaven","count":72,"share":0.29},{"strong":"G3772","lemma":"οὐρανός","xlit":"ouranós","gloss":"the sky","kjv":"air, heaven, sky","count":65,"share":0.26},{"strong":"G1093","lemma":"γῆ","xlit":"gē","gloss":"soil","kjv":"country, earth, ground, land","count":20,"share":0.08},{"strong":"G3962","lemma":"πατήρ","xlit":"patḗr","gloss":"a \"father\"","kjv":"father, parent","count":22,"share":0.09},{"strong":"G2362","lemma":"θρόνος","xlit":"thrónos","gloss":"a stately seat","kjv":"seat, throne","count":14,"share":0.06},{"strong":"G932","lemma":"βασιλεία","xlit":"basileía","gloss":"royalty","kjv":"kingdom, + reign","count":14,"share":0.06}],"verses":["Gen.1.1","Gen.2.1","Gen.19.24","Deut.26.15","1Sam.2.10","1Kgs.8.27","1Kgs.8.30","1Kgs.8.39","1Kgs.8.43","1Kg